sions is an app that makes decisions fun & easy! Just input your question, add/import options, and spin the wheel to get a random answer. Make quick decisions!\nL69: It’s always so hard to decide. Should I get a pizza or a burger? Should I get it in grey or black? Should I do this or should I do something else? The Tiny Decisions app is created just for you!\nL70: Features:\nL71: * Create your own customized decisions\nL72: * Touch to decide\nL73: * Built-in decision templates\nL74: * Set weight for options\nL75: * Select non-repeating options\nL76: * Color themes for wheel\nL77: Please write a review if you like this app, it's very important to me.\nL78: X: @tinydecisions\nL79: Mail: tangsuanhq@gmail.com\nL80: Happy deciding.\nL81: \nL82: Updated on\nL83: \nL84: Oct 18, 2026\nL85: \nL86: Entertainment\nL87: ## Data safety\nL88: \nL89: arrow_forward\nL90: \nL91: Safety starts with understanding how developers collect and share your data. Data privacy and security practices may vary based on your use, region, and age. The developer provided this information and may update it over time.\nL92: \nL93:   * 【21†Image: Icon image†play-lh.googleusercontent.com】\nL94: \nL95: No data shared with third parties\nL96: \nL97: 【22†Learn more†support.google.com】 about how developers declare sharing\nL98: \nL99:   * 【23†Image: Icon image†play-lh.googleusercontent.com】\nL100: This app may collect these data types\nL101: \nL102: Location, App activity and 2 others\nL103: \nL104:   * 【24†Image: Icon image†play-lh.googleusercontent.com】\nL105: \nL106: Data is encrypted in transit\nL107: \nL108:   * 【25†Image: Icon image†play-lh.googleusercontent.com】\nL109: \nL110: You can request that data be deleted\nL111: \nL112: See details\nL113: ## Ratings and reviews\nL114: \nL115: Ratings and reviews are verified info_outline\nL116: \nL117: arrow_forward\nL118: \nL119: Ratings and reviews are verified info_outline\nL120: \nL121: phone_android Phone\nL122: \nL123: laptop Desktop\nL124: \nL125: tablet_android Tablet\nL126: \nL127: 3.4\nL128: \nL129: 4.34K reviews\nL130: \nL131: 5\nL132: \nL133: 4\nL134: \nL135: 3\nL136: \nL137: 2\nL138: \nL139: 1\nL140: \nL141: 【26†Image†play-lh.googleusercontent.com】\nL142: \nL143: A Google user\nL144: \nL145: more_vert\nL146: \nL147: February 14, 2020\nL148: Good for what it is. I like the idea and I use multiple wheels. I then paid for the no ads and ability to add a weight to the items. I'm disappointed that I still get ads, but at least i can add the weight. I'd want a refund if I paid more than a dollar, but beware if you want no ads, don't bother buying it. Edit: app was just updated and all the wheels I had previously made were deleted and I had to restore my purchase using the weight option (settings didn't work)\nL149: \nL150: 86 people found this review helpful\nL151: Did you find this helpful?\nL152: \nL153: Yes\nL154: \nL155: No\nL156: \nL157: TS Tech\nL158: \nL159: February 21, 2020\nL160: \nL161: I've added a restore button on purchase page. Please have a try when you reinstall the app or download the app on your other devices.\nL162: \nL163: 【27†Image†play-lh.googleusercontent.com】\nL164: \nL165: Shandra Plourde\nL166: \nL167: more_vert\nL168: \nL169: December 31, 2024\nL170: ADHD helper - I have 42 things to do and I'm so overwhelmed. I put them all on my wheel and spin! I do whatever it lands on for as long as I can stand then spin again. Turning items on and off is very helpful; I'm not going to start something really dirty if it's almost bed time. I have a wheel for indoor and another for outdoor things depending on the weather. I don't mind the ads even a little. A good trade off. I think it's 10 spins or saving your item list then it gives you one.\nL171: 36 people found this review helpful\nL172: \nL173: Did you find this helpful?\nL174: \nL175: Yes\nL176: \nL177: No\nL178: \nL179: 【28†Image†play-lh.googleusercontent.com】\nL180: \nL181: Kermit the Hermit\nL182: \nL183: more_vert\nL184: \nL185: August 12, 2022\nL186: Everything about this app is amazing except for 2 things for me. 1. A dark mode setting would be fantastic, I've seen alot of reviews about this and I completely agree that a dark mode would improve this app 2. The sound doesn't work. I only hear the clicking and ding sound when a choice is selected by the wheel from my notification sound, not my media sound. I confirmed this by turning off my notification sound and having media all the way up. No sound at all. Please try to fix soon\nL187: 60 people found this review helpful\nL188: \nL189: Did you find this helpful?\nL190: \nL191: Yes\nL192: \nL193: No\nL194: \nL195: See all reviews\nL196: \nL197: 【29†flagFlag as inappropriate†support.google.com】\nL198: \nL199: 【9†Image: Content rating†play-lh.googleusercontent.com】\nL200: \nL201: Everyone\nL202: \nL203: 【10†Learn more†support.google.com】\nL204: ## App support\nL205: \nL206: expand_more\nL207: \nL208: 【30†public Website†tinydecisions.app】\nL209: \nL210: email Support email nix1024@gmail.com\nL211: \nL212: 【31†shield Privacy Policy†tinydecisions.app】\nL213: \nL214: About the developer\nL215: \nL216: 杭州糖蒜网络科技有限公司\nL217: \nL218: nix@tangsuan.tech\nL219: \nL220: 中国 浙江省杭州市 拱墅区湖州街701号502室025工位 邮政编码: 310000\nL221: \nL222: +86 195 2164 3075\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n‎Tiny Decisions: Spin Wheel - Ratings & Reviews - App Store (https://apps.apple.com/us/app/tiny-decisions-spin-wheel/id1338769645?see-all=reviews)\nciteturn13view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/tiny-decisions-spin-wheel/id1338769645?see-all=reviews\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 410\nL0: Search [Input]\nL1: \nL2:   * 【0†Today】\nL3:   * 【1†Games】\nL4:   * 【2†Apps】\nL5:   * 【3†Arcade】\nL6: \nL7: Platform\nL8: \nL9:   * 【0†iPhone】\nL10:   * 【4†iPad】\nL11:   * 【5†Mac】\nL12:   * 【6†Vision】\nL13:   * 【7†Watch】\nL14:   * 【8†TV】\nL15: \nL16: # 【9†Tiny Decisions: Spin Wheel】\nL17: ## Ratings & Reviews\nL18: \nL19:   * 4.7\nL20: \nL21: out of 5\nL22: \nL23: 90K Ratings\nL24: \nL25:   * ### Perfect for the indecisive. Best app ever\nL26: \nL27:     1.     2.     3.     4.     5. 05/31/2020\nL28: \nL29: Tyler Furnando\nL30: I have a problems committing to decisions. Leaving my choices (book to read, film to watch, game to play, etc bucketlist things) up to fate using this app really makes it easier. The wheel that supports hundreds and hundreds of options is great, and the non-repeating choice feature is awesome.\nL31: The backup/restore feature is very reliable- my particular set of “wheels” (with options greyed out and all accounted for) has lasted me through several phones and many factory resets.I also use this app as a way to count the total of books/films that I have backlogged, as it conveniently shows you the total number of options you have right there in the options.\nL32: My only complaint is that the “greyed out” / “non-repeating” options that are chosen aren’t marked in any way that I can tell when editing my wheel- it would be nice to even have a little asterisk put on it for accountability sake. But this hasn’t been an issue so far and they still always remain greyed out on wheel itself.TLDR: to me, this is the best, most feature rich, and stable app to help remedy decision-related OCD. i’m very glad it exists.\nL33: # Perfect for the indecisive. Best app ever\nL34: \nL35:     1.     2.     3.     4.     5. 05/31/2020\nL36: \nL37: Tyler Furnando\nL38: I have a problems committing to decisions. Leaving my choices (book to read, film to watch, game to play, etc bucketlist things) up to fate using this app really makes it easier. The wheel that supports hundreds and hundreds of options is great, and the non-repeating choice feature is awesome.\nL39: The backup/restore feature is very reliable- my particular set of “wheels” (with options greyed out and all accounted for) has lasted me through several phones and many factory resets.I also use this app as a way to count the total of books/films that I have backlogged, as it conveniently shows you the total number of options you have right there in the options.\nL40: My only complaint is that the “greyed out” / “non-repeating” options that are chosen aren’t marked in any way that I can tell when editing my wheel- it would be nice to even have a little asterisk put on it for accountability sake. But this hasn’t been an issue so far and they still always remain greyed out on wheel itself.TLDR: to me, this is the best, most feature rich, and stable app to help remedy decision-related OCD. i’m very glad it exists.\nL41:   * ### Get Pro -- it's worth it.\nL42: \nL43:     1.     2.     3.     4.     5. 03/12/2020\nL44: \nL45: CrazyWriterPerson01\nL46: I am an indecisive person surrounded by other equally indecisive people, so I tend to use this app quite heavily.\nL47: At only $1.99 for the Pro upgrade, it was really a no-brainer (honestly, I don't even remember what features are added with Pro because I upgraded almost as soon as I downloaded), and has saved me and my friends/family a LOT of time that would otherwise be spent in back-and-forths of, \"I dunno -- what do /you/ wanna do?\" I also love that you get to watch the wheel spin rather than just hit a button and have the choice appear onscreen (and that you can adjust the weight of each option and see the difference on the wheel).\nL48: It's more fun that way. And having the coin flip and eenie-meenie-minie-moe modes makes it an all-in-one app for all kinds of decisions. Things like being able to choose a color theme or a custom icon for each list are just added bonuses.\nL49: # Get Pro -- it's worth it.\nL50: \nL51:     1.     2.     3.     4.     5. 03/12/2020\nL52: \nL53: CrazyWriterPerson01\nL54: I am an indecisive person surrounded by other equally indecisive people, so I tend to use this app quite heavily.\nL55: At only $1.99 for the Pro upgrade, it was really a no-brainer (honestly, I don't even remember what features are added with Pro because I upgraded almost as soon as I downloaded), and has saved me and my friends/family a LOT of time that would otherwise be spent in back-and-forths of, \"I dunno -- what do /you/ wanna do?\" I also love that you get to watch the wheel spin rather than just hit a button and have the choice appear onscreen (and that you can adjust the weight of each option and see the difference on the wheel).\nL56: It's more fun that way. And having the coin flip and eenie-meenie-minie-moe modes makes it an all-in-one app for all kinds of decisions. Things like being able to choose a color theme or a custom icon for each list are just added bonuses.\nL57:   * ### Love it and have some suggestions...\nL58: \nL59:     1.     2.     3.     4.     5. 02/04/2019\nL60: \nL61: Nicheblon\nL62: This app is amazing! It can simply be used to choose for you or play a game of chance with friends, but it can also help you organize. I use this app everyday after school to randomize the order of things I need to do. It has many unique features like adding weight to specific options and even has a flip-a-coin option as well. The only I might recommend changing is the upgrade. I don’t see the necessity.\nL63: It doesn’t offer much in addition to what comes for free, and I don’t think the app should have adds in the first place because of how simple it is and how little it does.\nL64: Considering the amount of money the upgrade costs, I would still do it because it’s worth it to add weight to options in your lists, but I propose that you just let the app come with these “upgrades”.Overall, I think this app is amazing I just hope you keep my suggestions in mind because if you do decide to make them a permanent addition to the app, I think the app will be much more appreciated.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n‎Spin The Wheel - Random Picker - Ratings & Reviews - App Store (ht